#. Tag: title
#: security.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kppp; and security issues"
msgstr "&kppp; i sigurnosna pitanja"

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section is mainly for superusers (<systemitem>root</systemitem>) people "
"with high security demands, or simply technically interested people. It is "
"not necessary to read this if you only use &Linux; at home for yourself, "
"although you may learn a thing or two in any case."
msgstr ""
"Ovo poglavlje je uglavnom za superkorisnike (<systemitem>korijen</"
"systemitem>) sa visokim sigurnosnim zahtjevima, ili jednostavno tehnički "
"zainteresiranim ljudima. Ovo nije neophodno pročitati ukoliko samo koristite "
"&Linux; kod kuće za sebe, iako biste mogli naučiti jednu ili dvije stvari u "
"svakom slučaju."

#. Tag: title
#: security.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restricting access to &kppp;"
msgstr "Ograničena prava pristupa &kppp;-u"

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A system administrator might want to restrict access as to who is allowed to "
"use &kppp;. There are two ways to accomplish this."
msgstr ""
"Administrator sistema bi mogao htjeti da ograniči prava pristupa onome kome "
"je dopušteno da koristi &kppp;. Dva su načina da se ovo postigne."

#. Tag: title
#: security.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restricting access with group permissions"
msgstr "Ograničavanje prava pristupa sa grupnim dozvolama"

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a new group (you might want to name it <systemitem>dialout</"
"systemitem> or similar), and put every user that should be allowed to use "
"&kppp; into that group. Then type at the prompt:"
msgstr ""
"Kreirajte novu grupu (mogli biste je nazvati <systemitem>dialout</"
"systemitem> ili slično), i stavite sve korisnike kojima bi trebalo biti "
"dozvoljeno korištenje &kppp; u tu grupu. Zatim unesite u konzolu:"

#. Tag: screen
#: security.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>#</prompt> <userinput><command>chown</command> <option>root.dialout</"
"option> <filename>/opt/kde/bin/kppp</filename></userinput>\n"
"<prompt>#</prompt> <userinput><command>chmod</command> <option>4750</option> "
"<filename>/opt/kde/bin/kppp</filename></userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<prompt>#</prompt> <userinput><command>chown</command> <option>root.dialout</"
"option> <filename>/opt/kde/bin/kppp</filename></userinput>\n"
"<prompt>#</prompt> <userinput><command>chmod</command> <option>4750</option> "
"<filename>/opt/kde/bin/kppp</filename></userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This assumes that &kde; was installed in <filename class=\"directory\"> /opt/"
"kde/</filename> and that your new group is named <systemitem>dialout</"
"systemitem>."
msgstr ""
"Ovo je pod pretpostavkom da je &kde; instaliran u <filename class=\"directory"
"\"> /opt/kde/</filename> i da je Vaša nova grupa nazvana "
"<systemitem>dialout</systemitem>."

#. Tag: title
#: security.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restricting access &kppp;'s way"
msgstr "Ograničavanje prava pristupa na &kppp; način"

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before doing anything, &kppp; checks if there is a file named <filename>/etc/"
"kppp.allow</filename>. If such a file exists, only users named in this file "
"are allowed to dial out. This file must be readable by everyone (but of "
"course <emphasis>NOT</emphasis> writable.) Only login names are recognized, "
"so you cannot use <acronym>UID</acronym>'s in this file. Here is a short "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Prije nego išta uradite, &kppp; provjerava da li postoji datoteka pod imenom "
"<filename>/etc/kppp.allow</filename>. Ukoliko takva datoteka postoji, samo "
"korisnicima imenovanim u ovoj datoteci je dopušteno biranje. Ova datoteka "
"mora biti čitljiva svakome (ali naravno <emphasis>NE</emphasis> otvorena za "
"pisanje.) Samo login imena su prepoznatljiva, tako da ne možete koristiti "
"<acronym>UID</acronym> u ovoj datoteci. Ovo je kratki primjer:"

#. Tag: screen
#: security.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# /etc/kppp.allow\n"
"# comment lines like this are ignored\n"
"# as well as empty lines\n"
"\n"
"fred\n"
"karl\n"
"daisy"
msgstr ""
"# /etc/kppp.allow\n"
"# linije komentara kao ova se ignorišu\n"
"# kao i prazne linije\n"
"\n"
"fred\n"
"karl\n"
"daisy"

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the example above, only the users <systemitem>fred</systemitem>, "
"<systemitem>karl</systemitem> and <systemitem>daisy</systemitem> are allowed "
"to dial out, as well as every user with a <acronym>UID</acronym> of 0 (so "
"you don't have to explicitly list root in the file)."
msgstr ""
"U primjeru iznad, samo korisnicima <systemitem>fred</systemitem>, "
"<systemitem>karl</systemitem> i <systemitem>daisy</systemitem> je dozvoljeno "
"da biraju, kao i svakom korisniku sa <acronym>UID</acronym> sa 0 (tako da ne "
"morate eksplicitno navoditi korijen u datoteci)."

#. Tag: title
#: security.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kppp; has the <acronym>SUID</acronym> bit on? What about security?"
msgstr "&kppp; ima <acronym>SUID</acronym> bit uključen? Šta je sa sigurnosti?"

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It's virtually impossible to write a dialer without the <acronym>SUID</"
"acronym> bit that is both safe and easy to use for inexperienced users. "
"&kppp; addresses the security issues with the following strategy."
msgstr ""
"Praktično je nemoguće da upišete pozivaoca bez <acronym>SUID</acronym> bita "
"koji je i siguran i lagan za korištenje neiskusnim korisnicima. &kppp; "
"adresira sigurnosna pitanja sa sljedećom strategijom."

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "Immediately after the program starts, &kppp; forks."
msgstr "Odmah nakon što se program pokrene, &kppp; se račva."

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The master process, which handles all the <acronym>GUI</acronym> operations "
"(such as user interaction), drops the <acronym>SUID</acronym> state after "
"the fork, and runs with normal user privileges."
msgstr ""
"Glavni proces,  koji upravlja svim <acronym>GUI</acronym> operacijama (kao "
"što je korisnička interakcija), ispušta <acronym>SUID</acronym> stanje nakon "
"račvanja i pokreče se sa normalnim korisničkim privilegijama."

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The slave process keeps its privileges, and is responsible for all actions "
"that need <systemitem>root</systemitem> privileges. To keep this part safe, "
"no &kde; or &Qt; library calls are used here, just simple library calls. The "
"source code for this process is short (around 500 lines) and well "
"documented, so it's easy for you to check it for security holes."
msgstr ""
"Podređeni proces zadržava svoje privilegije, i odgovoran je za sve akcije "
"koje trebaju <systemitem>korijen</systemitem> privilegije. Da se ovaj dio "
"održi sigurnim,  ni jedan &kde; ni &Qt; poziv biblioteke se ovdje ne "
"korisni, samo jednostavne čelije biblioteke. Izvorni kod za ovaj proces je "
"kratak (oko 500 linija) i dobro dokumentovan, tako da Vam je jednostavno "
"provjeriti ima li sigurnosnih rupa."

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Master and slave processes communicate with standard &UNIX; <acronym>IPC</"
"acronym>."
msgstr ""
"Glavni i podređeni procesi komuniciraju sa strandardnim &UNIX; <acronym>IPC</"
"acronym>."

#. Tag: para
#: security.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Special thanks to Harri Porten for writing this excellent piece of code. It "
"was thought to be impossible, but he managed it within a week."
msgstr ""
"Specijalne zahvalnice Harri Portenu za pisanje ovog odličnog koda. Mislilo "
"se da je nemoguće, ali je on to uspio u roku od sedmicu dana."
